* Summary

This branch adds ~62 new HTTP endpoints across 11 new onboarding controllers,
plus extends 3 existing module API interfaces and adds 1 new one.  The
onboarding module alone adds roughly the same number of endpoints as the rest of
the application combined.

Six new Spring events are introduced.

The rest of this document lists every new or changed endpoint and module API,
grouped by domain, with a one-line description of each.

* Onboarding - Starter Work
  Path: `/api/v1/onboarding/starter-work`
  Controller: `StarterWorkController` (13 endpoints)

**Admin / PM / HR surface**

- `POST /generate` → ADMIN,PM,HR
  Triggers AI mining over the project’s ingested open tracker issues.  Mined
  tasks are stored LIVE and claimable immediately.  Returns
  `GenerateStarterWorkResponse`.

- `POST /generate/stream` → ADMIN,PM,HR (SSE)
  Streaming twin — watch the pool fill one task at a time as
  `Flow<AiProgressEvent>`.

- `POST /` → ADMIN,PM
  Create a hand-authored starter-work task with no AI in the loop.  Body:
  `CreateStarterWorkTaskRequest`.

- `GET /candidates` → ADMIN,PM,HR
  Lists a project’s open ingested tracker issues for browsing.  Deterministic
  filter, no AI call.  Param: `projectId`.  Returns
  `List<StarterWorkCandidateResponse>`.

- `POST /candidates/promote` → ADMIN,PM
  Puts a browsed issue into the pool as live + reviewed.  Body:
  `PromoteStarterWorkCandidateRequest`.

- `GET /unreviewed` → ADMIN,PM
  Live tasks no PM has vouched for yet.  Already claimable; reviewing lifts only
  a fit-ranking demotion.

- `GET /pool` → ADMIN,PM
  The entire live starter-work pool.

- `POST /{id}/review` → ADMIN,PM
  Mark a task reviewed (idempotent).

- `POST /{id}/reject` → ADMIN,PM
  Remove a task from the pool permanently — mining never re-proposes it.  Body
  (optional): `RejectProposalRequest`.

**Hire self-serve surface (`/me/...`)**

- `GET /me/matches` → USER
  Ranks the live pool by fit for the authenticated hire.  Deterministic, no AI.
  Returns `List<RankedStarterWorkTaskResponse>` with reasons per task.

- `POST /me/goal` → USER
  Claims a task as the hire’s goal.  Body: `ClaimGoalRequest`.  Returns
  `GoalView`.

- `DELETE /me/goal` → USER
  Drops the hire’s goal; falls back to baseline.

* Onboarding - Task Orientation
  Path: `/api/v1/onboarding`
  Controller: `TaskOrientationController` (7 endpoints)

AI-assembled (or human-authored) task guidance grounded in the project corpus.

**Hire self-serve**

- `GET /me/orientation` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  AI-assembled orientation for the caller’s current task, cached against the
  corpus.  Param: `projectId`.  Returns `MyOrientationResponse`.

- `POST /me/orientation/stream` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN (SSE)
  Streaming twin.  Returns `Flow<AiProgressEvent>`.

- `PUT /me/orientation` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  Fix the caller’s orientation in place with hand-authored content.  Pins as
  HUMAN origin.  Body: `AuthorOrientationRequest`.  Returns
  `OrientationPacketResponse`.

- `DELETE /me/orientation` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  Revert to AI assembly for the caller’s task.

**PM authoring**

- `GET /orientation/tasks/{taskId}` → PM,ADMIN
  Read a task’s orientation for editing; never triggers AI generation.

- `PUT /orientation/tasks/{taskId}` → PM,ADMIN
  Author a task’s orientation (PM-side).  Body: `AuthorOrientationRequest`.

- `DELETE /orientation/tasks/{taskId}` → PM,ADMIN
  Restore AI assembly for a task (PM-side).

* Onboarding - Buddy
  Path: `/api/v1/onboarding/me/buddy`
  Controller: `BuddyController` (5 endpoints)

A persistent, tool-using, streaming AI companion conversation per hire.

- `GET /messages` → USER
  The caller’s buddy conversation so far, oldest first.  Returns
  `List<BuddyMessageResponse>`.

- `GET /suggestions` → USER
  Quick-question chips drawn from the tools mounted for this hire.  No model
  call.  Returns `List<BuddySuggestionResponse>`.

- `POST /open/stream` → USER (SSE)
  Opens a visit — folds prior visit into memory, streams a proactive greeting.
  Returns `Flow<BuddyStreamEvent>`.

- `POST /messages` → USER (SSE)
  Sends a message and streams the grounded reply.  Body:
  `SendBuddyMessageRequest`.  Returns `Flow<BuddyStreamEvent>`.

- `POST /actions` → USER
  Confirms a buddy-proposed action (start Task 0, claim goal, flag to PM, etc.).
  Body: `BuddyActionRequest`.  Returns `BuddyActionResponse`.

Buddy stream event vocabulary: `tool_use`, `token`, `citation`, `action_proposal`,
`done`, `error`.

* Onboarding - Board
  Path: `/api/v1/onboarding`
  Controller: `BoardController` (6 endpoints)

A per-hire, per-project card surface with 11 card types discriminated by
`BoardCardKind`.

- `GET /me/board` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  The caller’s board on a project.  Created on first read.  Param: `projectId`.
  Returns `BoardResponse`.

- `GET /me/board/cards/{cardId}/diagram` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  Redraw a diagram card if the project has changed; returns cached otherwise.

- `POST /me/board/cards` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  Add a user-authored card (note, link, checklist).  Body: `AuthoredCardRequest`.
  Returns `BoardCardResponse`.

- `PATCH /me/board/cards/{cardId}` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  Edit a user-authored card’s content.  Body: `AuthoredCardRequest`.

- `PUT /me/board/order` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  Reorder cards.  Body: `ReorderBoardRequest` (list of card IDs in order).

- `DELETE /me/board/cards/{cardId}` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  Dismiss a card permanently.  Idempotent.

Board card content types:
- `PATH_TO_FIRST_CONTRIBUTION` — timeline moments (joined→claimed→submitted→responded→accepted)
- `ARRIVAL_STEPS` — what still needs to be true before the hire can work
- `OPEN_PULL_REQUESTS` — open PRs with wait times
- `CURRENT_TASK` — the hire’s current task, or the fact they have none
- `SUGGESTED_TASKS` — ranked fit suggestions with reasons
- `COMPETENCY_PROGRESS` — held vs in-progress competencies
- `MEMORY_RECAP` — the mentor’s durable memory note
- `DIAGRAM` — an AI-drawn architecture diagram grounded in project material
- `NOTE` — user-authored free text
- `LINK` — user-authored URL
- `CHECKLIST` — user-authored checklist with tickable items

* Onboarding - Arrival Steps

**Authoring**
  Path: `/api/v1/onboarding/arrival-steps`
  Controller: `ArrivalAuthoringController` (6 endpoints)

- `GET /` → ADMIN,PM,HR
  List steps in a scope (optional `projectId`; omit for company-wide).

- `POST /` → ADMIN,PM
  Create a step.  Body: `CreateArrivalStepRequest`.

- `GET /derivable` → ADMIN,PM,HR
  List steps the system can verify for itself (e.g. GitHub account exists).

- `PATCH /{key}` → ADMIN,PM
  Update a step’s wording, link, or settlement mechanism.  Key is immutable.

- `POST /reorder` → ADMIN,PM
  Apply a complete ordering.  Body: `ReorderArrivalStepsRequest`.

- `DELETE /{key}` → ADMIN,PM
  Delete a step definition.  Hire settlement records survive by key.

**Hire self-serve**
  Path: `/api/v1/onboarding`
  Controller: `MyArrivalController` (3 endpoints)

- `GET /me/arrival` → USER
  The caller’s steps across all projects + company-wide, counted by rigor.
  Returns `MyArrivalResponse`.

- `POST /me/arrival/refresh` → USER
  Re-checks observable steps (GitHub account, work produced).

- `POST /me/arrival/{key}/confirm` → USER
  Self-confirm a step (DECLARED rigor).  Idempotent.

* Onboarding - Attestations
  Path: `/api/v1/onboarding`
  Controller: `AttestationController` (6 endpoints)

Work confirmed by a named colleague, for roles nothing observes.

- `GET /me/attestations` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  The caller’s attestation requests on a project.  Param: `projectId`.

- `POST /me/attestations` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  Ask someone to confirm your work.  Body: `RequestAttestationRequest`.

- `POST /me/attestations/{id}/withdraw` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  Withdraw a request you no longer want answered.

- `GET /attestations/pending` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  What is waiting on the caller to confirm, longest-waiting first.

- `POST /attestations/{id}/accept` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  Confirm the work happened and met the bar.

- `POST /attestations/{id}/send-back` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  Send back with what needs to change.  Body: `SendBackAttestationRequest`.

* Onboarding - Competencies
  Path: `/api/v1/onboarding`
  Controller: `MyCompetencyController` (1 endpoint)

- `GET /me/competencies` → USER
  The caller’s full durable competency ledger (level + source per competency).
  Returns `List<MyCompetencyResponse>`.

* Onboarding - Knowledge Requests
  Path: `/api/v1/onboarding`
  Controller: `KnowledgeRequestController` (7 endpoints)

The buddy’s growth loop: escalate a gap to a PM, answer it, serve the answer
as durable knowledge.

- `GET /me/knowledge-requests` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  The caller’s own escalated questions.

- `POST /me/knowledge-requests` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  Escalate a question the buddy could not answer.  Body: `CreateKnowledgeRequest`.

- `GET /knowledge-requests` → PM,HR,ADMIN
  The escalation inbox for a project.  Param: `projectId`.

- `POST /knowledge-requests/{requestId}/answer` → PM,ADMIN
  Answer an escalated question (mints a durable canonical answer).  Body:
  `AnswerKnowledgeRequest`.

- `POST /knowledge-requests/{requestId}/dismiss` → PM,ADMIN
  Close without minting an answer.

- `GET /canonical-answers` → PM,HR,ADMIN
  Every durable answer on a project.  Param: `projectId`.

- `PUT /canonical-answers/{answerId}` → PM,ADMIN
  Edit a canonical answer.  Body: `UpdateCanonicalAnswer`.

* Onboarding - Task Zero
  Path: `/api/v1/onboarding`
  Controller: `TaskZeroController` (3 endpoints)

The trivial first task that proves the branch→PR→review→merge loop.

- `POST /starter-work/{proposalId}/task-zero` → ADMIN,PM
  Flag an approved task as suitable for Task 0.  Body:
  `SetTaskZeroEligibilityRequest`.

- `GET /me/task-zero` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  Read (and auto-assign, if the hire’s environment is ready) the caller’s Task
  0.  Param: `projectId`.  Returns `MyTaskZeroResponse`.

- `DELETE /me/task-zero` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  Undo a Task 0 assignment.  Frees the task for someone else.

* Onboarding - Metrics
  Path: `/api/v1/onboarding/metrics`
  Controller: `OnboardingMetricsController` (4 endpoints)

Time-to-first-merged-PR, response latency, and stalls.

- `GET /me` → USER,PM,HR,ADMIN
  The caller’s own onboarding timeline.  Returns `HireTimelineResponse`.

- `GET /projects/{projectId}` → ADMIN,PM,HR
  Project-level metrics: medians, p90s, stalls, per-hire timelines.

- `GET /projects/{projectId}/users/{userId}` → ADMIN,PM,HR
  One hire’s timeline.

- `GET /projects/{projectId}/attention` → ADMIN,PM,HR
  Who needs a human today — open PRs kept waiting, stalls found.

* User module - Project Roles (new endpoints)
  Path: `/api/v1/admin`
  Controller: `ProjectRoleController` (3 new endpoints)

- `GET /projects/{projectId}/users/{userId}/project-roles` → ADMIN,PM,HR
  The roles a user holds on one project.

- `POST /projects/{projectId}/users/{userId}/project-roles` → ADMIN,PM,HR
  Assign a role to a user, gated by project membership.

- `DELETE /projects/{projectId}/users/{userId}/project-roles/{roleId}` → ADMIN,PM,HR
  Remove a role from a user, gated by project membership.

* Module API interfaces (internal)

**UserApi — 6 new methods**

- `getGithubLoginByUserId(userId)` → `String?`
  The GitHub account a user contributes as.
- `getDeclaredSkills(userId)` → `List<DeclaredSkill>`
  Skills a user has self-declared with level.
- `getGithubSeedingContext(userId)` → `GithubSeedingContext?`
  Everything the GitHub-history seeder needs in one read.
- `setGithubSeedingConsent(userId, consentedAt)`
  Opt in or out of work-history calibration.
- `setGithubLogin(userId, githubLogin)` → `String`
  Record/update a user’s GitHub username.
- `recordGithubLoginVerification(userId, verification)`
  Record whether GitHub confirmed the login exists.

**GithubRepositoryApi — 3 new methods**

- `getRepositoryIdsByProject(projectId)` → `List<UUID>`
  All repository connections for a project.
- `getSourceInstances(projectId?)` → `List<GithubSourceInstanceDto>`
  Connected repositories for status reporting.
- `removeProjectFromAllRepositories(projectId)`
  Cleanup on project deletion.  Idempotent.

**ArtifactIngestionApi — ~10 new methods**

- `getAuthoredWork(projectId, authorLogin)` → `List<AuthoredArtifact>`
  What one GitHub account has authored in a project’s ingested corpus.
- `getAuthoredPullRequests(projectId, authorLogin)` → `List<AuthoredPullRequest>`
  Pull request lifecycle data for one author.
- `getAssignedIssues(projectId, assigneeDisplayName)` → `List<AssignedIssue>`
  Tracker issues assigned to one person, with lifecycle timestamps.
- `getTaskSource(sourceId)` → `TaskSourceArtifact?`
  The artifact text a starter-work task was mined from.
- `getOpenIssues(projectId)` → `List<IngestedIssue>`
  Every open tracker issue in a project’s corpus.
- `getIssue(sourceId)` → `IngestedIssue?`
  One ingested issue by source id, open or not.
- `getRepositoryResponsiveness(projectId)` → `List<RepositoryResponsiveness>`
  Median response time per repository from ingested data.
- `exists(artifactId)` / `existsInProject(projectId, artifactId)`
  Existence checks.
- `getHash(artifactId)` / `getFirstIngestedAt(component)` (batch variant)
  Cached metadata lookups.
- `findArtifactById(artifactId)` → `ArtifactDto?`
  Full artifact retrieval.

**ProjectMembershipApi — new interface**

- `getProjectMembers(projectId)` → `List<ProjectMember>`
  Everyone on a project with displayName, githubLogin, joinedAt, and
  jiraDisplayName.

**New Spring events**

- `UserDeletedEvent` — fired when a user is deleted; cleans up onboarding data
- `UserSessionStartedEvent` — fired on authenticated request traffic; marks
  session activity for idle detection

@end